   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result:** at θ_A = θ_F + 2h the only B-eigen words are the 16 F-only words (a₁ = a₃ = 0), and **B itself is degenerate**: 169 = 13² distinct eigenvalues (B invertible, rank 256). No word basis can be B-diagonal there; the rank-169 collapse of the u_A = θ_A − h words is the same phenomenon.\n\n### Where is B degenerate? Distinct eigenvalues vs d = θ_A − θ_F (pair-locked, θ_F generic)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "nDistinctB[d_] := Module[{B1, B2, ev},\n   setTheta[{-3/5 + d, -3/5, -11/8 + d, -11/8}]; B1 = Bop[37/100]; B2 = Bop[-113/100];\n   ev = Eigenvalues[N[B1 + 7/10 B2, 40]]; Length[Union[Round[ev, 10^-20]]]];\ndRows = Table[{d, nDistinctB[d]}, {d, {0, hh, 2 hh, 3 hh, 4 hh, 2 hh + 1/10, 1/3}}];\nGrid[Prepend[dRows, {\"d = θ_A − θ_F\", \"# distinct eigenvalues of B (of 256)\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
