      {
       "data": "Out[892]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{d = $\\theta$\\_A − $\\theta$\\_F} & \\text{\\# distinct eigenvalues of B (of 256)}\\\\\\hline0 & 256\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{2} & 169\\\\\\hline1 & 169\\\\\\hline\\frac{3}{2} & 169\\\\\\hline2 & 256\\\\\\hline\\frac{11}{10} & 256\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{3} & 256\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "6f931ab5-c288-4bd6-995b-dd67e1079630"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result:** B(u) (RV gl(4), untwisted T) has simple spectrum for d = θ_A − θ_F ∈ {0, 4h, generic} but only **169 = 13² distinct eigenvalues at d ∈ {h, 2h, 3h}** — the separated variables of the A and F site of a pair collide. The ABJM point d = 2h lies in this resonant window, so the RV SoV basis does not exist there as a B-eigenbasis; the shifted word bases (u_A = θ_A − 3h, θ_A + 2h) are bases but not SoV (only the 16 F-only words are B-eigen). The sparse BPS expansions (earlier cells) at generic θ are in a genuine SoV basis (all 256 words B-eigen).\n\nOptions: approach the ABJM point as a limit d → 2h of the generic SoV basis (singular measure/normalisation), or use a different B (e.g. built from the 4̄ auxiliary space or another frame) whose separated variables do not collide at d = 2h.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Convention check: is our ⟨0| the Ryan–Volin SoV vacuum?\n\nRV (arXiv:2002.12341) (4.12): ⟨0| is the lowest-weight (GT) vacuum, characterised by (3.19): ⟨0|T_{j1}(u) = δ_{j1}ν(u)⟨0| for j = 1..4, with the untwisted monodromy (RV Lax u − ħΣE_ij⊗π(E_ji), T = ℒ_L⋯ℒ₁; ours u − θ + hΣe_ij⊗ρ(E_ij), T = ℒ₁⋯ℒ_L, so π = −ρᵀ and our site s is RV's site 2L+1−s). Test: common left kernel of T₂₁, T₃₁, T₄₁ (two u values) and T₁₁-eigen condition, compared with our ⟨0| = e₁⊗e₄⊗e₁⊗e₄; generic θ and the ABJM θ.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "vacCheck[thNew_] := Module[{T1, T2, K, kern, ourRes},\n   setTheta[thNew]; T1 = Tun[37/100]; T2 = Tun[-113/100];\n   K = Join[Transpose[T1[[2, 1]]], Transpose[T1[[3, 1]]], Transpose[T1[[4, 1]]], Transpose[T2[[2, 1]]], Transpose[T2[[3, 1]]], Transpose[T2[[4, 1]]]];\n   kern = NullSpace[K];\n   (* T11-eigen condition within the kernel *)\n   kern = Select[kern, MatrixRank[{#, # . T1[[1, 1]]}] == 1 &];\n   ourRes = {Normal[vac . T1[[2, 1]]] == ConstantArray[0, 256] && Normal[vac . T1[[3, 1]]] == ConstantArray[0, 256] && Normal[vac . T1[[4, 1]]] == ConstantArray[0, 256], MatrixRank[{vac, vac . T1[[1, 1]]}] == 1};\n   {Length[NullSpace[K]], Length[kern], If[Length[kern] == 1, MatrixRank[{First[kern], vac}] == 1, \"n/a\"], ourRes}];\nvacRows = {{\"generic θ\", Sequence @@ vacCheck[{2/7, -3/5, 8/11, -11/8}]}, {\"ABJM θ (θ_A = θ_F + 2h)\", Sequence @@ vacCheck[{-3/5 + 2 hh, -3/5, -11/8 + 2 hh, -11/8}]}};\nGrid[Prepend[vacRows, {\"θ\", \"dim common left kernel of T₂₁,T₃₁,T₄₁\", \"# of those T₁₁-eigen (single vectors)\", \"= our ⟨0| ?\", \"our ⟨0|: {T_{j1} kills it (j>1), T₁₁-eigen}\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
