   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result:** (3.19) alone leaves a 15-dim kernel (it characterises the embedded subspace). The full GT-vacuum condition — ⟨0| killed by every strictly lower-triangular T_{ij}(u), i > j (the recursive (3.19) through the embeddings φ: T_{ij} → T_{i+1,j+1}), and eigen of every T_{ii} — has a **one-dimensional solution, equal to our ⟨0| = e₁⊗e₄⊗e₁⊗e₄**, at generic θ and at the ABJM θ (exact). So our SoV vacuum is the Ryan–Volin one (A site = RV's dual irrep, lowest weight e₁; F site = RV's fundamental, lowest weight e₄). Since B has simple spectrum at generic θ and all 256 words are B-eigen, the words coincide with RV's basis (4.12) up to normalisation. RV's genericity assumption (2.9) θ_α − θ_β ∉ ħℤ is violated at the ABJM point (θ_A − θ_F = 2h), consistent with the B degeneracy found above.",
